<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Alcoa of Australia to cut capitalisation.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Alcoa of Australia to cut capitalisation.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alcoa of Australia Ltd said on Friday it planned to reduce its capitalisation by A$300 million.</p>
<p>The funds would be distributed to shareholders, the company said in a statement.  </p>
<p>Alcoa said the funds would be distributed in line with ownership ratios.</p>
<p>Aluminium Co of America would receive A$180 million, gold and base metals miner WMC Ltd A$117.75 million and Australian insurance group QBE Ltd, A$2.24 million.</p>
<p>Alcoa said its shareholders would consider the proposal on March 6. Shareholders' equity after the reduction would be about A$1.60 billion.</p>
</text>
